/* SEO GUIDE COPY. Edit freely, then run: node build.js
   Each line is: ["target keyword", "section heading", "paragraph"]. Add more lines to add more paragraphs. */
const SEO={
"web-design":[["web design agency","Choosing a web design agency","A good web design agency asks about your customers before it talks about colors. Look for a portfolio with clear results, a defined process and a plan for content and SEO. Ask who will write the copy, because words often matter more than visuals."],["responsive design","Why responsive design still matters","Responsive design adapts a website to any screen size. Many visitors arrive on phones, so layouts, text and buttons must work with a thumb. Test on real devices, not only a browser preview, to catch problems early."],["UX design","What UX design adds to a website","UX design shapes how easily people can complete a task on your site. It covers navigation, page order and forms. Small improvements here can have more effect than a new visual style."],["small business website","What a small business website needs","A small business website needs clear services, proof, contact details and fast pages. Skip anything that doesn't help a customer decide. A focused site is cheaper to run and easier for local search engines to understand."],["Next.js website","When a Next.js website makes sense","A Next.js website suits businesses wanting strong performance and flexibility. It can deliver fast pages and connect to a headless CMS. It needs developer support, so weigh that against simpler options."]],
"redesign":[["website redesign company","What to ask a website redesign company","Ask a website redesign company how it protects traffic during launch. A strong answer includes content mapping, redirects and post-launch monitoring. Also ask how it will measure whether the new site performs better."],["redirect mapping","Why redirect mapping protects SEO","Redirect mapping connects every important old URL to the best new page. Without it, visitors hit errors and search engines lose signals. Build the map before launch, then test it on staging."],["website migration","Planning a website migration","A website migration moves your site to a new platform, domain or structure. Plan the timing away from busy seasons, keep a full backup and watch Search Console closely after launch."],["website refresh","When a website refresh is enough","A website refresh updates visuals, copy and key pages without a full rebuild. It suits sites with sound structure and technology. It's faster and cheaper, and it may deliver most of the benefit."],["website modernization","Modernizing an aging website","Website modernization replaces old technology and outdated patterns. It often improves security, speed and accessibility as well as appearance. Start with the pages that matter most to revenue."]],
"rapid":[["startup website","What a startup website needs first","A startup website needs a clear promise, a reason to believe and one next step. You don't need every page at launch. Ship quickly, talk to users, then improve the message as you learn."],["website sprint","How a website sprint works","A website sprint compresses planning, copy, design and build into a short window. It relies on a single decision maker and daily feedback. Fewer meetings mean faster progress."],["one-page website","When a one-page website works","A one-page website suits a single offer, event or early-stage product. It's quick to build and easy to read. As your services grow, separate pages will help you rank for more search terms."],["MVP website","Launching an MVP website","An MVP website contains the minimum needed to test demand. Measure what visitors click and ask, then decide what to build next. This avoids spending money on features nobody wants."],["fast website design","What makes fast website design safe","Fast website design stays safe through limited scope, tested components and clear ownership. Cutting quality checks isn't the answer. Keep accessibility, speed and basic SEO on the list, even with a tight deadline."]],
"ecom-design":[["online store design","Principles of online store design","Good online store design makes the path to purchase obvious. Use clear categories, honest product information and visible delivery costs. Every extra click should earn its place."],["product page design","What strong product page design includes","Strong product page design combines clear images, key benefits, price, stock and reviews. Put the buy button where people expect it, and answer common doubts before they have to ask."],["checkout optimization","Simple checkout optimization wins","Checkout optimization starts by removing surprises. Show delivery fees early, offer guest checkout and keep forms short. Local payment options can also make a large difference."],["cart abandonment","Understanding cart abandonment","Cart abandonment happens for many reasons, including unexpected costs and slow pages. Some shoppers are only comparing. Fix the avoidable causes first, then use reminders for the rest."],["mobile commerce","Designing for mobile commerce","Mobile commerce needs large tap targets, quick loading and digital wallets. Filters should be easy to use with one hand. Test your entire purchase path on an ordinary phone."]],
"landing-pages":[["PPC landing pages","Why PPC landing pages need their own design","PPC landing pages match the promise of your ad, which helps relevance and conversion. Paid clicks are costly, so remove anything that distracts from the offer."],["high-converting landing page","Parts of a high-converting landing page","A high-converting landing page has a clear headline, relevant proof, a strong offer and one call to action. Length depends on the decision. Bigger commitments usually need more reassurance."],["A/B testing","A/B testing landing pages properly","A/B testing compares two versions with real traffic. Change one meaningful thing, wait for enough conversions, and avoid stopping early. Record what you learn for future campaigns."],["message match","What message match means","Message match means your page repeats the promise of the ad or email that brought the visitor. It reassures people that they're in the right place, and it reduces instant exits."],["lead generation page","Designing a lead generation page","A lead generation page trades something useful for contact details. Make the value clear and ask only for what you need. Explain what happens after someone submits the form."]],
"web-dev":[["web development company","Choosing a web development company","When you choose a web development company, ask about testing, documentation and code ownership. Check how they handle hosting and support after launch. These matter long after the design is forgotten."],["Next.js development","Benefits of Next.js development","Next.js development offers fast pages, server rendering and good SEO foundations. It's especially useful when content and app features live together. Skilled developers are needed to get the best from it."],["headless CMS","Pros and cons of a headless CMS","A headless CMS separates content from presentation, so one source can feed several channels. It offers flexibility, but it requires more setup than traditional platforms. Editors need good previews."],["Core Web Vitals","Improving Core Web Vitals","Core Web Vitals measure loading, responsiveness and layout stability. Compress images, reduce JavaScript and reserve space for media. Better scores help users, and they support search performance."],["custom web development","When custom web development is worthwhile","Custom web development is worthwhile when templates limit your business. It costs more up front, but it can fit your workflows exactly. Check that the extra value justifies long-term maintenance."]],
"wordpress":[["custom WordPress theme","Benefits of a custom WordPress theme","A custom WordPress theme includes only what your site needs. That usually means better speed and fewer conflicts than a multipurpose theme. It also matches your brand exactly."],["Gutenberg blocks","Building with Gutenberg blocks","Gutenberg blocks let editors assemble pages from approved components. Custom blocks keep design consistent while giving marketers freedom. They also avoid the weight of many page builders."],["WordPress speed","Practical WordPress speed fixes","WordPress speed improves with good hosting, caching, image compression and fewer plugins. Measure before and after each change. Often, a single heavy plugin is responsible for most of the delay."],["headless WordPress","Is headless WordPress right for you?","Headless WordPress keeps the familiar editor while a modern front end displays content. It can be fast and flexible, but it adds complexity. It suits teams with developer support."],["WordPress maintenance","Why WordPress maintenance matters","WordPress maintenance keeps core, themes and plugins up to date. Skipped updates are a common way sites get compromised. Test changes on staging, and keep regular backups."]],
"ecom-dev":[["Shopify development","What Shopify development covers","Shopify development includes themes, apps and integrations. Many stores need only a clean theme and a few trusted apps. Custom work makes sense when the business has special requirements."],["headless commerce","When headless commerce pays off","Headless commerce gives complete control over the storefront. It suits large or complex brands. For most stores, the extra cost and maintenance won't be justified."],["payment gateway integration","Choosing payment gateway integration","Payment gateway integration affects trust and conversion. Offer methods your customers use locally, check fees, and test refunds as well as purchases. Security and compliance must be handled properly."],["inventory integration","Why inventory integration matters","Inventory integration keeps stock levels accurate across channels. It prevents overselling and saves manual updates. Decide which system is the master record before building."],["WooCommerce development","What WooCommerce development offers","WooCommerce development gives full control on top of WordPress. It's flexible and well suited to content-heavy stores. You'll need good hosting and regular maintenance."]],
"web-apps":[["client portal development","Benefits of client portal development","Client portal development gives customers a secure place for files, invoices and updates. It reduces routine emails and looks professional. Start with the information clients ask for most."],["dashboard development","Good dashboard development","Good dashboard development starts with the decisions people need to make. Show fewer numbers, clearly. Filters and exports should support real tasks rather than decoration."],["MVP development","Why MVP development reduces risk","MVP development builds the smallest useful product to test your idea. Real feedback guides what comes next. This lowers risk and keeps early budgets under control."],["internal tools","When to build internal tools","Build internal tools when spreadsheets slow your team or create errors. Small custom tools can repay their cost quickly. Consider low-code options for simple cases."],["role-based access","Designing role-based access","Role-based access gives each user only the data and actions they need. It reduces risk and makes interfaces simpler. Plan roles early, because adding them later can be painful."]],
"cms":[["content modeling","What content modeling means","Content modeling defines the types of content you have and how they relate. Good models avoid copy and paste, and they make redesigns easier. Plan them before building pages."],["Sanity CMS","When to consider Sanity CMS","Sanity CMS is a flexible headless platform with customizable editing. It suits teams wanting structured content and modern front ends. Compare it with other options on pricing and editor needs."],["CMS migration","Running a CMS migration","A CMS migration moves content, media and URLs to a new platform. Audit first, because some content shouldn't move. Plan redirects and preserve metadata to protect search visibility."],["multi-site CMS","Managing a multi-site CMS","A multi-site CMS runs several websites from one system. It helps brands share components and control consistency. Local teams still need permission to adapt content."],["Webflow CMS","Is Webflow CMS a good fit?","Webflow CMS suits marketing sites that need strong design control without much code. It's less suitable for complex applications. Review limits on items and integrations before committing."]],
"security":[["website security audit","What a website security audit checks","A website security audit reviews software versions, access, configuration and known vulnerabilities. The result should be a prioritized fix list. Repeat it after major changes."],["web application firewall","How a web application firewall helps","A web application firewall filters harmful traffic before it reaches your site. It blocks many automated attacks. It doesn't replace patching, but it adds a useful layer."],["malware removal","Safe malware removal steps","Malware removal means cleaning infected files and finding how attackers got in. Change all passwords and review admin users. Without fixing the cause, the infection usually returns."],["website backup","Building a reliable website backup","A website backup is only useful if it can be restored. Store copies away from your server, automate them, and test recovery. Know how much data you can afford to lose."],["SSL certificate","What an SSL certificate does","An SSL certificate encrypts traffic between visitors and your site. Browsers warn users when it's missing. It's essential, but it doesn't protect against every type of attack."]],
"maintenance":[["website care plan","What a website care plan includes","A website care plan usually covers updates, backups, monitoring and a set number of support hours. Read what's excluded, and check response times before signing."],["managed hosting","Why choose managed hosting","Managed hosting takes care of servers, updates and basic security. It costs more than cheap shared plans, but it can save time and prevent outages."],["uptime monitoring","Setting up uptime monitoring","Uptime monitoring checks your site regularly and alerts you to problems. Monitor key pages and forms, not just the home page. A fast alert limits lost business."],["CDN setup","How CDN setup improves speed","A CDN stores copies of your files around the world, closer to visitors. That improves load times and can reduce server strain. Configure caching carefully for dynamic pages."],["website retainer","When a website retainer makes sense","A website retainer gives you regular access to help for fixes and improvements. It suits businesses making frequent changes. Agree on priorities and turnaround times."]],
"conversion":[["CRO agency","What a CRO agency should do","A CRO agency should begin with research, not random tests. Ask for examples of hypotheses, test results and learning. Good partners report on revenue and qualified leads."],["heatmaps","Using heatmaps wisely","Heatmaps show where people click and scroll. They reveal ignored content and false buttons. Treat them as clues, then confirm with analytics and user feedback."],["conversion audit","What a conversion audit reveals","A conversion audit reviews data, pages and forms to find the biggest leaks. The outcome is a ranked list of fixes, so you know where to begin."],["funnel optimization","Where to begin funnel optimization","Funnel optimization starts at the step with the largest drop-off and highest value. Fix one stage at a time, so that you can see what caused any change."],["user research","Why user research beats guessing","User research explains why people behave as they do. Short surveys, interviews and usability tests reveal doubts that analytics can't show. It's especially useful on low-traffic sites."]],
"funnels":[["marketing funnel","Understanding the marketing funnel","A marketing funnel describes stages from awareness to purchase. Real buyers don't always move in a straight line, but the model shows where to focus content and offers."],["GoHighLevel funnels","Building GoHighLevel funnels","GoHighLevel funnels combine pages, forms, messaging and pipelines. They suit agencies and service businesses. Keep flows simple and respect consent for texts and calls."],["booking funnel","Designing a booking funnel","A booking funnel takes a visitor straight to a calendar. Explain what happens on the call, qualify lightly and send reminders. Fewer steps usually mean more booked meetings."],["webinar funnel","What a webinar funnel needs","A webinar funnel needs a useful topic, a simple sign-up, reminders and follow-up. Most value often comes from the replay and the conversations afterward."],["lead magnet funnel","Creating a lead magnet funnel","A lead magnet funnel exchanges something helpful for contact details. Solve one specific problem, and connect it to your paid offer through a follow-up sequence."]],
"lead-gen":[["B2B lead generation","How B2B lead generation differs","B2B lead generation involves longer cycles and several decision makers. Useful content, targeted outreach and strong follow-up matter more than volume. Measure pipeline, not just form fills."],["qualified leads","Defining qualified leads","Qualified leads match your target profile and show real intent. Agree on the definition with sales, then review it regularly. Clarity here prevents most marketing and sales disputes."],["lead nurturing","Why lead nurturing matters","Lead nurturing keeps in touch with prospects who aren't ready yet. Helpful emails, content and timely check-ins keep you in mind until the moment is right."],["demand generation","Demand generation vs. lead capture","Demand generation builds awareness before people are looking. Lead capture collects those already looking. Healthy pipelines usually need both, with budgets adjusted over time."],["appointment setting","What good appointment setting looks like","Appointment setting books qualified meetings for your sales team. Quality matters more than quantity. Agree on criteria, and review no-show and close rates together."]],
"marketing-auto":[["HubSpot automation","Getting value from HubSpot automation","HubSpot automation can manage lists, emails and lifecycle stages. Keep workflows documented and named well. Audit regularly, because old rules often conflict with new campaigns."],["drip campaigns","Writing effective drip campaigns","Drip campaigns send planned messages over time. Each email should have one purpose. Stop the sequence once someone responds, so that people don't get irrelevant messages."],["customer journey","Mapping the customer journey","A customer journey map shows the stages people move through and what they need at each. It reveals gaps in your messaging, and guides what to automate first."],["behavioral email","Using behavioral email triggers","Behavioral email sends messages based on actions such as visiting pricing or downloading a guide. Timing makes it relevant. Use these triggers with care, and respect privacy preferences."],["SMS automation","When SMS automation fits","SMS automation suits reminders and urgent updates. Keep messages short, get clear consent, and follow local rules. Too many texts quickly lead to opt-outs."]],
"analytics":[["GA4 setup","Getting GA4 setup right","GA4 setup should begin with the questions you want answered. Define key events, filter internal traffic and link your ad accounts. A clean setup saves confusion later."],["Google Tag Manager","Keeping Google Tag Manager tidy","Google Tag Manager lets you deploy tags without code changes. Use clear names and folders, and limit access. Old tags should be removed, because they can slow your site."],["server-side tracking","Benefits of server-side tracking","Server-side tracking routes data through your own endpoint. It gives more control and can improve data quality. It still has to respect user consent and privacy laws."],["attribution","Making sense of attribution","Attribution assigns credit for a conversion across marketing touchpoints. No model is perfect. Use it to compare trends, and combine it with CRM data for a truer picture."],["Looker Studio","Building Looker Studio dashboards","Looker Studio turns marketing data into shareable dashboards. Start with the few metrics leaders need. Too many charts hide the story that you're trying to tell."]],
"personalization":[["dynamic content","Getting started with dynamic content","Dynamic content changes parts of a page depending on the visitor. Start with headlines or proof sections. Keep a strong default version for anyone who doesn't match a segment."],["B2B personalization","What B2B personalization looks like","B2B personalization can show industry examples or relevant case studies. Company data can guide this. Keep it helpful, and avoid naming individuals in a way that feels intrusive."],["first-party data","Why first-party data matters","First-party data comes directly from your own audience. It's more reliable and easier to use responsibly than third-party data. Explain clearly how you collect and use it."],["geo-targeting","Using geo-targeting well","Geo-targeting adapts content by location, including language, offers and contact details. It's simple and often effective. Make sure search engines can still access every version."],["personalized landing pages","When to use personalized landing pages","Personalized landing pages match an ad or email segment. They work well for high-value campaigns. Start with a few segments, because too many versions become hard to maintain."]],
"reviews":[["Google reviews","How to get more Google reviews","More Google reviews usually come from simply asking real customers at the right moment. Send a direct link, keep it short, and don't offer incentives that break the rules."],["reputation management","What reputation management involves","Reputation management tracks and responds to what people say about you online. It means fixing real problems as well as replying. You can't honestly remove fair criticism."],["review automation","Keeping review automation honest","Review automation sends requests after a purchase or service. Ask everyone equally, so you don't filter out unhappy customers. Check each platform's rules before you start."],["customer testimonials","Collecting customer testimonials","Customer testimonials are strongest when they're specific and include a real name, with permission. Ask what changed for them. Never invent or edit a quote's meaning."],["local reviews","Why local reviews matter","Local reviews influence both customer decisions and local search visibility. Reply to them, and use the feedback to improve. Recent reviews tend to reassure buyers more."]],
"abm":[["target account list","Building a target account list","A target account list names the companies you most want to win. Use fit, revenue potential and intent signals. Sales must agree with it, or the program won't work."],["buying committee","Mapping the buying committee","A buying committee includes everyone who influences a B2B purchase. Identify champions, finance and technical reviewers, then give each one the information they need."],["LinkedIn ABM","Using LinkedIn ABM campaigns","LinkedIn ABM campaigns can target people at named companies. Use a matched list, and rotate useful content. Smaller audiences need careful frequency control."],["sales and marketing alignment","Improving sales and marketing alignment","Sales and marketing alignment depends on shared goals, definitions and regular reviews. ABM helps by giving both teams the same list. Celebrate pipeline together."],["account engagement","Measuring account engagement","Account engagement tracks activity across a company, not one person. Look for several people showing interest. That's often a stronger buying signal than a single form fill."]],
"sf-auto":[["Salesforce Marketing Cloud","Is Salesforce Marketing Cloud right for you?","Salesforce Marketing Cloud suits organizations with large audiences and complex journeys. It's powerful but requires expertise. Check product names and packaging, since Salesforce updates them often."],["Account Engagement","Getting more from Account Engagement","Account Engagement, formerly Pardot, supports B2B nurture and scoring. Clean connector settings and clear scoring rules matter most. Sales should help define what a good lead looks like."],["Journey Builder","Designing with Journey Builder","Journey Builder creates automated paths based on behavior and data. Keep journeys simple at first. Test entry rules carefully, because one mistake can reach many contacts."],["campaign attribution","Setting up campaign attribution","Campaign attribution shows how marketing influences Salesforce opportunities. It relies on consistent campaign membership and contact roles. Without those habits, reports won't reflect reality."],["Salesforce consultant","When to hire a Salesforce consultant","A Salesforce consultant helps when your setup has grown complex or adoption is low. Look for relevant certifications and real marketing experience, not just administration."]],
"channel":[["deal registration","Why deal registration matters","Deal registration lets partners claim opportunities and avoids conflict. Set clear rules and fast approval. Partners will only use it if it protects them and gets answered quickly."],["partner relationship management","What partner relationship management covers","Partner relationship management includes onboarding, training, leads, deals and reporting. Simple tools work best for dealers. Start with what partners need most."],["dealer network","Supporting a dealer network","A dealer network needs fast leads, good marketing assets and clear territories. For heavy equipment, parts and service enquiries matter as much as new sales."],["lead distribution","Fair lead distribution rules","Lead distribution sends enquiries to the right partner by territory or skill. Set a response deadline, then reassign unanswered leads. Fair rules keep partners engaged."],["channel sales","Measuring channel sales","Channel sales reporting should show deals by partner, stage and region. Consistent definitions matter, so train partners well. Reward those who keep the pipeline up to date."]],
"email":[["email deliverability","Improving email deliverability","Email deliverability depends on authentication, sender reputation and engagement. Set up SPF, DKIM and DMARC, remove inactive contacts, and send content that people want."],["email list growth","Healthy email list growth","Email list growth should come from real interest. Offer something useful in exchange for a sign-up. Never buy lists, because they damage reputation and may break the law."],["B2B email marketing","What works in B2B email marketing","B2B email marketing works when it's useful and specific. Short emails with one idea tend to perform well. Different roles need different messages, so segment your list."],["Klaviyo agency","When to use a Klaviyo agency","A Klaviyo agency can help ecommerce brands build flows and segments. Look for experience with your store's platform and for reporting based on revenue."],["email campaigns","Planning email campaigns","Email campaigns work best when they follow a plan linked to your business calendar. Give each send one goal, and review results to shape the next one."]],
"campaigns":[["email segmentation","Getting started with email segmentation","Email segmentation groups contacts by behavior or interest. Even simple segments, such as customers versus prospects, improve relevance. Add more detail only when you have content to match."],["email copywriting","Email copywriting that gets read","Email copywriting should sound like one person writing to another. Keep subject lines clear and specific. Lead with what the reader gets, and use one main call to action."],["email reporting","What to look for in email reporting","Email reporting should focus on clicks, conversions and revenue. Open rates can be unreliable because of privacy features. Compare results by segment for useful insight."],["send time","Finding the best send time","The best send time depends on your audience. Test different days and times, then look for consistent patterns. Relevance usually matters more than the exact hour."],["promotional email","Writing a promotional email","A promotional email should make the offer obvious quickly. Be honest about terms and deadlines. Too many promotions wear out a list, so balance them with useful content."]],
"email-auto":[["welcome series","Writing a welcome series","A welcome series introduces your brand when interest is high. Deliver what you promised, share your story, and suggest a next step. Keep each email focused."],["abandoned cart email","What makes an abandoned cart email work","An abandoned cart email reminds shoppers what they left behind. Send it soon, show the product and answer common doubts. Discounts aren't always needed."],["win-back email","Writing a win-back email","A win-back email tries to re-engage people who've gone quiet. Ask if they still want to hear from you. Removing those who don't respond protects deliverability."],["post-purchase email","The value of post-purchase email","Post-purchase email reassures buyers and reduces support questions. Share delivery details and tips for using the product. Later, ask for a review or suggest a related item."],["nurture sequence","Building a nurture sequence","A nurture sequence educates leads over time. Answer common questions, share proof, and invite a next step. Make sure that it stops when someone becomes a customer."]],
"newsletter":[["B2B newsletter","Creating a B2B newsletter people read","A B2B newsletter earns attention by being useful to readers' jobs. Share practical ideas, not just company news. A consistent format makes it easy to read quickly."],["newsletter growth","Practical newsletter growth","Newsletter growth comes from clear value and visible sign-ups. Promote it on your website and social channels. Asking readers to share a good issue can also help."],["editorial calendar","Using an editorial calendar","An editorial calendar plans topics and deadlines ahead. It keeps your newsletter consistent and reduces last-minute stress. Leave room for timely news."],["newsletter writing","Tips for newsletter writing","Newsletter writing works best with a clear point of view. Write to one reader, use short sections, and let your personality show. Facts and examples build credibility."],["beehiiv","Should you use beehiiv?","Beehiiv is a popular newsletter platform with growth and monetization tools. It suits publishers and creators. Businesses should compare it against their existing email and CRM systems."]],
"email-design":[["responsive email","Building responsive email","Responsive email adapts to phones and desktops. Use a single-column layout where possible, large buttons and readable text. Always test, because support varies by client."],["HTML email","Why HTML email is different","HTML email relies on older techniques than modern websites. Tables and inline styles are often needed for reliable results. Tools like MJML can simplify the process."],["dark mode email","Designing for dark mode email","Dark mode email can change your colors unexpectedly. Use transparent logos with care, and check contrast. Test in clients that invert colors, since each behaves differently."],["email accessibility","Improving email accessibility","Email accessibility helps everyone read your message. Use real text, alt text, good contrast and clear links. Don't hide key information inside an image."],["A/B test email","How to A/B test email","To A/B test email, change one element and use a large enough audience. Measure clicks or sales when possible. Keep a record of results, so that learning builds."]]
};

